{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And YHWH appeared in the Tent in a pillar of cloud</b>: The explanation is that the pillar of cloud was at the entrance, and HaShem was seen in the Tent — and this is the Glory, according to the opinion of R. Abraham ibn Ezra (on Deuteronomy 31:15). In my opinion it is like <b>and YHWH descended in a pillar of cloud and stood at the entrance of the Tent</b> (Numbers 12:5), and <b>behold, the glory of YHWH appeared in the cloud</b> (Exodus 16:10). The explanation is that He wished to speak with Moses in a manner that Joshua would hear, and there He would give command to Joshua himself. Now, to Moses it was said (Exodus 25:22), <b>and I will meet with you there and speak with you from above the cover</b>, but Joshua was not at that level and it was forbidden for him to enter the Tent at all. And so <b>and the pillar of cloud stood at the entrance of the Tent</b> comes back to explain that the cloud — and in it the Glory — was at the entrance of the Tent, hovering over it, yet He was in the Tent."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:15.623938239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}